  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity-building and strategic planning support</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project was launched during the 20th anniversary year of Asia Muslim Action Network (AMAN), when CAFOD agreed to support a process whereby the network could re-visit their vision, mission, goals and objectives, taking in where they&#x2019;ve come from and considering what challenges they will face in the future.  This process created an opportunity to review AMAN&#x2019;s portfolio of programmes, especially their peace education work, and to look at whether they were reaching their intended outcomes, how their focus has evolved, and what priorities should be set for the future.  A continuation of funding during 2011-12 included some support to AMAN&#x2019;s organisational overheads; this continuation was to allow further time to engage in strategic planning, building on the outcomes of the 2010 evaluation.  
In 2012 -13 we began investigating how AMAN&#x2019;s programmes can better support our work in other countries more strategically, particularly Sri Lanka, Afghanistan, Bangladesh &amp; South East Asia. Whilst this process continues we have pledged a further instalment of support to their core costs.</narrative>
  </description>
